rties (SAN, issuer) as a self-check. Ponytail says non-trivial logic needs a self-check. gen-certs can verify with openssl x509:\n    - trusted server SAN contains DNS:osaka-server and verify against ca\n    - untrusted server verify against trusted ca fails\n    - wronghost SAN lacks osaka-server\n  Add simple asserts using `openssl verify` and `openssl x509 -checkhost`.\n  `openssl x509 -in cert -noout -checkhost osaka-server` returns 0 if matches.\n  `openssl verify -CAfile ca.crt trusted/server.crt` 0; `openssl verify -CAfile ca/ca.crt untrusted/server.crt` nonzero.\n  Print generated paths.\n- Security: keys mode 600. umask 077.\n- Don't write to repo: caller passes temp dir; but ensure output dir is not repo? The script can just use provided dir; run-a10 uses mktemp. Could refuse if inside repo? Not necessary but nice: check path not under repo? Task says \"运行时用 openssl 生成临时 CA 与证书到临时目录，不入库\". We can require output dir and recommend mktemp. No need extra.\n\nDocker compose specifics. Let me write it carefully.\n\n```yaml\n# 用途：A10 端到端拓扑 —— 服务端以 docker 服务名 osaka-server 提供 HTTPS，管理端 probe 从另一容器经 docker 网络查询。\n# 前置环境：GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest + docker compose；证书由 gen-certs.sh 在运行时生成，经 CERTS_DIR 挂载。\n# 运行命令：由 run-a10.sh 调用（docker compose ... up/run）；不要单独起。\n# 覆盖 acceptance：A10。\n# 待写手交付后对齐：server 启动命令、probe 可执行文件/镜像/Dockerfile 路径（见下方 ${...} 默认值）。\n# 不发布宿主机端口、不使用 network_mode: host，避免走本机回环。\n\nx-notes: ...\nservices:\n  osaka-server:\n    image: python:3.12-slim\n    working_dir: /workspace\n    command: [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"exec ${SERVER_CMD:-python -m server}\"]\n```\n\nWait: environment substitution in compose with `${SERVER_CMD:-python -m server}` works. But using `sh -c` and string. If SERVER_CMD contains spaces, as a single string after exec, shell splits it, fine.\n\n```yaml\n    volumes:\n      - ${OSAKA_ROOT:-../..}/server:/workspace/server:ro\n      - ${CERTS_DIR:?CERTS_DIR required}:/certs:ro\n    environment:\n      OSAKA_TLS_CERT: /certs/${OSAKA_CERT_