eady ensured healthy. Keep.\n\nToken: compose requires `OSAKA_ADMIN_TOKEN` and `PROBE_TOKEN`. run-a10 exports both. In case 2, set PROBE_TOKEN to wrong token. But environment variable exported from shell for compose substitution. `OSAKA_ADMIN_TOKEN` correct always.\n\nCould pass `environment` override via `docker compose run -e OSAKA_ADMIN_TOKEN=wrong`. But compose interpolation already needed PROBE_TOKEN at parse time. Set env before invocation: `PROBE_TOKEN=\"$WRONG\" docker compose run ...`. Exported? Inline env assignment applies to command. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `docker compose run` triggers compose config interpolation; OSAKA_ADMIN_TOKEN required. run-a10 exports it. Fine.\n\nNow run-a10.sh details with functions. Let me write:\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ... header ...\nset -euo pipefail\numask 077\n\nHERE=$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\nROOT=$(cd \"$HERE/../../..\" && pwd)\nCOMPOSE_FILE=\"$HERE/docker-compose.yml\"\n\n# ---- 待写手交付后对齐（集中在这里；产品入口变化只改这里） ----\nSERVER_DIR=\"$ROOT/server\"\nADMIN_DIR=\"$ROOT/admin\"\nCOMPOSE_PROJECT=\"${COMPOSE_PROJECT:-osaka-a10}\"\nPROBE_URL=\"https://osaka-server:8443\"   # 任务卡固定：服务名 + 8443\nSERVER_SERVICE=\"osaka-server\"\nPROBE_SERVICE=\"osaka-probe\"\nPROBE_BIN=\"${PROBE_BIN:-/app/probe}\"    # 待对齐：probe 可执行文件路径\nPROBE_DOCKERFILE=\"${PROBE_DOCKERFILE:-admin/Dockerfile.probe}\"  # 待对齐\nTEST_ADMIN_TOKEN=\"${TEST_ADMIN_TOKEN:-osaka-test-fake-token-0000}\"  # 明显假值\nWRONG_TOKEN=\"wrong-token-obviously-fake\"\nPROBE_OK=0                       # 待对齐：probe 成功退出码\nCONNECTED_MARKER=\"${CONNECTED_MARKER:-已连接}\"   # 待对齐：已连接显示文案\nOK_MARKER_REGEX=\"${OK_MARKER_REGEX:-(version|health|健康|版本)}\"  # 待对齐：版本/健康显示文案\n# ②③④ 判定：退出码非 0 且输出不含 CONNECTED_MARKER。若写手定义了细分退出码，可在此登记。\n```\n\nHmm, \"按退出码判定四项\" — our cases 2-4 check nonzero. That's by exit code. Good.\n\nDelivery check:\n```bash\nmissing=()\n[ -d \"$SERVER_DIR\" ] || missing+=(\"server/\")\n[ -d \"$ADMIN_DIR\" ] || missing+=(\"admin/\")\nif [ ${#missing[@]} -gt 0 ]; then\n  echo \"待测：模块未交付（缺少 ${missing[*]}）\"\n  exit 0\nfi\ncommand -v docker >/dev/null || { echo \"缺少 docker，A10 端到端需在 GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest + docker 运行（待 CI）\" >&2; exit 2; }\ndocker compose version >/dev/null ...\n```\n\nWait, should \"待测：模块未交付\" be exactly that phrase. Yes.\n\nBut admin dir may exist partially without probe. Could check `[ -f \"$ROOT/$PROBE_DOCKERFILE\" ]` too. The task says product code not delivered. If admin/ exists but no probe Dockerfile, it's not delivered for our test → output 待测. But if writer delivered with a different Dockerfile path, our default may be wrong; then we'd wrongly skip. We define variable top for alignment. Maybe don't skip based on Dockerfile because run will fail obviously. Better check admin dir + server dir. Skip.\n\nTemp & cleanup:\n```bash\nTMP=$(mktemp -d)\nexport CERTS_DIR=\"$TMP/certs\"\nexport OSAKA_ROOT=\"$ROOT\"\nexport OSAKA_ADMIN_TOKEN=\"$TEST_ADMIN_TOKEN\"\nexport PROBE_BIN PROBE_DOCKERFILE PROBE_URL\ncleanup() {\n  docker compose -p \"$COMPOSE_PROJECT\" -f \"$COMPOSE_FILE\" down -v --remove-orphans >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n  rm -rf \"$TMP\"\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\n\"$HERE/gen-certs.sh\" \"$CERTS_DIR\"\n```\nNote gen-certs prints.\n\nFunction wait_server:\n```bash\nstart_server() { # $1 = cert set\n  OSAKA_CERT_SET=\"$1\" docker compose -p \"$COMPOSE_PROJECT\" -f \"$COMPOSE_FILE\" up -d --force-recreate --wait \"$SERVER_SERVICE\"\n}\n```\nNeed OSAKA_CERT_SET exported for compose parse. Inline env assignment works.\n\nRun probe:\n```bash\nrun_probe() { # $1 token\n  set +e\n  output=$(PROBE_TOKEN=\"$1\" OSAKA_CERT_SET=trusted docker compose -p ... run --rm \"$PROBE_SERVICE\" 2>&1)\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  printf '%s\\n' \"$output\"\n  return $rc  # but set -e in caller...\n}\n```\nActually easier: use if directly.\n\nLet me define `run_probe` that sets globals PROBE_OUT and PROBE_RC:\n```bash\nPROBE_OUT=\"\"\nPROBE_RC=0\nrun_probe() {\n  local token=\"$1\"\n  set +e\n  PROBE_OUT=$(PROBE_TOKEN=\"$to