itHub Actions ubuntu-latest）\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n```\nExit 2 in CI would fail, which is right. Locally, product missing so we exit before this. Good.\n\nNow grep-guard's header and behavior.\n\nLet me write the files.\n\nOne more consideration: The task says \"运行环境 ubuntu-latest + docker\". Compose at repo root? Our compose is in tests/admin/admin-connect. In CI, paths relative. Fine.\n\nLet me create and test.\n\nAlso, should the docker-compose.yml define a network explicitly? Compose creates a default network. Task says docker network service name. Explicit network not needed. But \"不走本机回环\" — no port publishing. Good. Maybe add `networks: [osaka-a10]`? Not needed; default works and is minimal. Keep default.\n\nShould server expose 8443? No; containers communicate within the network; healthcheck uses port internally. No `ports` mapping. Good.\n\nNow, `command` for server: The python image's default CMD is python; our command overrides. Good.\n\nMaybe server needs `PYTHONUNBUFFERED` for logs. Add `PYTHONUNBUFFERED: \"1\"`. Good for CI debugging. Minimal.\n\nProbe service `depends_on` with health. Good.\n\nCould the probe's mounted CA path `/usr/local/share/ca-certificates/osaka-test-ca.crt` be read-only and `update-ca-certificates` needs to read it; fine. The directory may exist. Docker mounts the file; if the parent directory exists (ca-certificates package creates it). Yes.\n\nOne issue: mounting a single file into a path whose parent doesn't exist would create it. Fine.\n\nAlso set `HOME`? no.\n\nNow, `.NET` HttpClient on Linux uses `SSL_CERT_FILE` or system store after update. Good.\n\nLet me write.\n\nPotential issue: The extension of `gen-certs.sh` and its shebang. chmod +x needed. We'll chmod.\n\nNow write all four files.","signature":"3e3dc233-77c6-4440-8013-9a2ce302fda3"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3324,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":24960,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"contex