e uses `${PROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT:-${OSAKA_ROOT:-../../..}}`. Or simply `${PROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT:-../../..}` with default relative; run-a10 always exports absolute. Compose runs only via run-a10 per header. Use `${PROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT:-../../..}`. Good.\n\nAdd to run-a10 top:\n```\nPROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT=\"${PROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT:-$ROOT}\"\n```\nand export. Header note. Update compose.\n\nAlso, does `docker compose build` use the `OSAKA_ROOT`? It needs `PROBE_BUILD_CONTEXT`. Good.\n\nLet me apply.","signature":"b3963222-fbe3-4d4e-acfe-a5807170c5a2"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":74368,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85b5f7a4-f572-472d-8399-89c76017bd29","uuid":"1b11c098-3bb2-47c5-9e66-241fe350993e","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:06:07.307Z","thinking_duration_ms":3926,"thinking_display":"updates"}
